From: "Baptiste G." <70719480+BeeeFX@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:08:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Node graph: a node in error drawn in the error colour; a
 selected node keeps its colour

- nodeErrorTint and nodeErrorColor (Appearance > Node Graph > Node and link drawing; 0 by default, Natron's dark
  red frame and large ERROR as before): above 0, a node in error takes the error colour, with an outline and the
  frame in it, and its message shows when the mouse is over it (the large ERROR doesn't fit a compact node).
- nodeSelectedTint now brightens a selected node towards white, keeping its own colour, with an outline in the
  selection colour, instead of mixing it with the selection colour (a selected blue Merge turned brown).
- With postage stamps off (readerPreview), nothing renders an unconnected Read, so Natron never found a missing
  file: the Read now looks for its file when it's named (any file of a sequence pattern in its folder) and says
  "File not found" at once; the check waits for the node to be made (a node being made drops its messages).
- A node's drawing shows a message the node got before the drawing existed.
- Both new preferences are read by name, so Settings.h doesn't change.

Since the audit of 11 November 2026 (NAT-7): the Read's file check runs on a worker thread (the folder may
be on a network drive) and its answer comes back on the interface's; it tries the current frame, then the
sequence's first and last, before listing the folder; it knows %v and %V; it waits at most 50 turns for the
node to be made; and it never runs headless (a render says it anyway).

Core patch 0003 of the BeeeFX fork (layer/patches/), on top of 0001, written to be offered upstream as it is.

Gap: layer/GAPS.md, "Nuke's look and habits" (the node graph's drawing: errors and selection).
Size: 4 files, 211 lines added, 7 removed.
upstream: not offered yet (to offer to Niik-l with 0001: github.com/Niik-l/Natron).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
